Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-21-2000||01:32 PM||||Cliff makes an alarm system??  Where does he find the time?||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||05-21-2000||02:08 PM||||LOL! Good one Bastard! Probably a good idea though to add one in with the luck I've been having lately.||||reg||1
Z||000005||olympic||05-21-2000||08:39 PM||||   You'll like the pager feature.  Does it indicate on the pager what sensor has been tripped on the car?  Anyways, I'd recommend to anyone who buys an alarm to also buy a pager with it.  These days nobody cares if your alarm is wailing.  YOU need to know when the alarm has been tripped.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||05-22-2000||09:28 AM||||If your looking at one of the Sony Xplode Head Units with the "Rotary Encoder" knob on it.  DONT BUY IT....<P>IT WILL DRIVE YOU NUTS....<P>I have a Sony with the Rotary Encoder knob and after 6 months the thing went silly. You spin the wheel to turn volume down and not only does it not go down, but sometimes actually goes up...<P>So I sent it to Crutchfield and they fixed it no prob.  6 months later its doing the same thing again.  <P>Prior to my first round of problems, A friend of mine bought one for himself cuz he thought mine was cool.  His did the same thing after about 6-8 months.  But not before his girlfriend and her mother thought they were pretty cool radios and bought themselves each one as well.  Both of those are acting up now too.<P>It all fairness, these are not the Xplode series, but mine looks identical except it does not have the red trim.  I sincerely hope they have gotten better switches made for them.  My next headunit will be an Alpine or Kenwood.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Racer 1||05-22-2000||10:58 AM||||Ive had two sony's in my fiero in the past and both scratched my cd's evertime I loaded them in the cd player. I finally got a Kenwood CD player and never had a problem again.<p>[This message has been edited by Racer 1 (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000008||TheFiero64||05-22-2000||11:25 AM||||I love my cd player. It is a factory delco unit. Here is the pic. It also lights up the same color as the rest of the dash.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CDrad.JPG"> <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000009||stimpy||05-22-2000||08:04 PM||||I'll stick up for Sony-san. I have had Sony products for my last 2 systems and found the to be excellent value. I have the rotary knob and it works fine. Pioneer makes the best tuners however...if you EVER listen to the radio, Alpines are useless! (unless your favorite station broadcasts from your trunk <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000010||RobH||05-22-2000||10:35 PM||||TheFiero64 --<P>Do you have the part # for that Delco stereo like you have?  I'm looking for something just like that - I want to keep the factory look.  I seem to remember having seen a link to that same cd player, but can't seem to find it.<P>Thanks...<BR>Rob||||reg||5
Z||000011||DJRice||05-23-2000||09:55 AM||||I guess I kind of ranted a bit too much about the sony.  I have a Sony head unit + Custom File Changer in my Grand Cherokee and it works like a champ.  Ive even got the wireless remote.  (for those back seat passengers who must have stereo control)<P>I had a Sony full logic casette deck w custom file changer in my Buick until someone relieved me of them both.  It worked like a champ for the 9 months I had it, and I recovered the car minus the radio)<P>Maybe they have improved those rotary knobs in the new models, I sure hope so.||||reg||1
